{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503186-rushing-to-become-a-master-or-spend-experience-on-multiple-arcana","id":1503186,"title":"Rushing to become a Master or spend experience on multiple Arcana?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-15T16:48:40-08:00","id":1503186,"title":"Rushing to become a Master or spend experience on multiple Arcana?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I remember that on 1ed that the game was breaking down at Adept level, but faced with the same decision on 2ed got met thinking on what is better, try to be a multiple adept vs rushing to become a master as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> I think it comes to the mechanical (what can you do) vs social part (respect by being a master), so with that being said:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>From a <b>respect/status/goodwill </b>standpoint<b>,</b> is it better to be a Master of a single arcana or a multiple degree Adept/Disciple? Put in another way, <b>what is the socially optimal way to spend XP on Arcana/Gnosis?</b></li> <li>From a <b>capabilities </b>standpoint, is it better to be a Master of a single arcana or a multiple degree Adept/Disciple? Put in another way, <b>what is the mechanically optimal way to spend XP on Arcana/Gnosis?</b></li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T17:20:00-08:00","id":1503193,"title":"","content":"Masters are rare, so they're better able to capitalize on their reputation as a potential teacher. Or even just as a potential weapon/tool.<br /> <br /> Multi-degree Adepts are better suited to creating novel effects that combine multiple Arcana. So while the Master can make phenomena up whole-cloth, the Adept twists many phenomena together in ways the Master can't. They're <i>better</i> than the Master in a lot of ways, but are still limited by their materials, where the Master isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T17:24:32-08:00","id":1503194,"title":"","content":"THe most socially optimally way to develop Arcana (and correspondingly Gnosis) is to develop enough of the right Arcana to ensure that you will always throw the best parties.<br /> <br /> Jokes asides.<br /> <br /> 1) Socially speaking, mastery is generally prized higher because masters overall are kind of rare due to scarcity(the long road of improving Gnosis and Arcana to that point), and you need a master to learn that 5th Dot for any Arcana not Ruled by your Path. No one will deny the utility and power of an Adept/Disciple, but that scarcity makes for a valuable resource.<br /> <br /> 2) The Actual Answer is &quot;However allows you to handle problems reliably and regularly&quot; and that doesn't even need magic, but realizing that we are still here, It's better to be an adept/ disciple of a handful of Arcana than a Master of one, which is part of the reason why Masters are rare. Obviously, spreading too thin is a problem.<br /> <br /> As an aside, if you imagine you're going to keep having questions about mage's society, it might pay to create a topic thread for that specifically for you keep things close-knit together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T17:32:41-08:00","id":1503195,"title":"","content":"As I said in the other thread, it will depend a great deal on the parameters of your setting but in general I would say masters get a lot of respect by virtue of mastery but multi-degree adepts are more likely to be the people who have spent time amassing institutional power. In pure EXP terms it would be more efficient putting the points into social merits.<br /> <br /> With respect to capabilities it will depend on what exactly you want to do. In terms of magical conflict there is an asymmetry between offence and defence, since the Practices of Veiling and Shielding are only 2 dots. Even a master is vulnerable in the arcana that they don't have. But no mage is an island and the best strategy is always to have an emotionally stable, reliable cabal with a diverse spread of arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T20:53:29-08:00","id":1503203,"title":"","content":"Rushing to Mastery is likely to get you some funny looks if you can't manage to swing a reputation and station where such a thing isn't perceived as a half-baked power-grab \u2014 I'd imagine the phenomenon is viewed not dissimilarly to characters outspokenly looking to form their own Legacies rather than join an established tradition. Unless you're racing toward being able to create rotes in the pursuit of an Obsession your peers consider useful, you're better off maintaining a more well-rounded spread of Arcana before pursuing the sort of major breakthroughs needed to raise your Gnosis to 5 or 6.<br /> <br /> From a perspective of raw practicality, any mage who hasn't at least dipped a toe into more than half the Arcana is short several Lesser Utility Attainments and probably has one or two gaping holes in their magical competencies. Having ratings that are too unbalanced also means you're working with a very brittle toolset for the Duel Arcane, which in turn means you're one bad roll away from not being able to open Doors with your singular best Arcanum in one of Awakened society's most persuasive conflict-resolution methods.<br /> <br /> Socially, while Masters are recognized for their skill, most Masters who are not PCs are not going to have attained that status by trying to become hyper-specialized. The Awakened tendency to act like magical jackdaws while they build up a favored style bears true here as well \u2014 just because your primary Obsession is in stretching the limits of Fate-based curses doesn't mean the ability to summon and bind the dead isn't also good to have, and most wizards recognize this because, even though the Arcana are recognized in-setting, the way mages learn magic requires them to engage with the supernatural in more concrete ways than the abstract notion of &quot;I need to raise my Prime rating.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T08:06:03-08:00","id":1503315,"title":"","content":"A multi degree Adept gets a lot more Greater Utility Attainments, which means things like Imbue Item, Time in a Bottle, Everywhere and so on. This means they are very versatile and likely able to provide more affordable services. So they would be more interesting politically.<br /> <br /> However, in terms of capabilities and gaining major boons, Masters have them beat. Focusing on doing a few things really well pays dividends in spades and overall gives more prestige.<br /> <br /> A master of Time can Unmake a target at sensory range by spending a mana, they can create a year's worth of preparation time to ritual cast a big spell at a moment's notice or they can allow you to complete months of intensive research instantly.<br /> <br /> Masters of Fate can simply decide that you succeed in any Supernal summonings of their choice, doing it faster and safer despite how complex it is. They can be a major boon in freeing people from gaeas and free bound souls without risking Paradox. They can decree that today you will get that big break on a cold case or difficult project. You call call them on the phone about anything and their seemingly random advice will not only wotk, but play perfectly to your strengths, giving them an air of omniscience.<br /> <br /> Masters of Prime can speak to people over the phone about the thing you saw but cannot prove and people will believe them, they will even mobilize them into action. They can create Hallows if they put in the effort, making them an invaluable source of mana. They can even prepare a ritual that will dispel all the defenses of a Sanctum away without risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> Masters of Space can create a stable portal network to multiple locations, giving you mobility that was previously undreamed of. They can create an area where spells cast within never risk Paradox. They can look at an unstoppable vampire juggernaut and decide to lock it in place via a Ban.<br /> <br /> Becoming a multi degree Adept means your talents will be in high demand, whether on the field or via crafting, which makes it easier to build a contact network. Being a Master will give you more prestige and will probably give you more standard and major boons to call upon.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}